<attribute name="mainDescription" nodeId="6656231f">&lt;p&gt;
    An evaluation of impacts with descriptions of the changes that have or may occur. Impacts may be evaluated both
    qualitatively and quantitatively.
&lt;/p&gt;</attribute>
<attribute name="externalId" nodeId="e8bde87b"></attribute>
<attribute name="keyConsiderations" nodeId="34227f01">Impacts may be driven by external forces such as new regulations.</attribute>
<attribute name="longPresentationName" nodeId="33d27f5e"></attribute>
<attribute name="purpose" nodeId="524a2bad">&lt;p&gt;
    To inform stakeholders about potential ramifications pertaining to categories such as economic, social, technology, or
    environment.
&lt;/p&gt;</attribute>
<attribute name="impactOfNotHaving" nodeId="e4f2ddc9"></attribute>
<attribute name="reasonsForNotNeeding" nodeId="5abb6f0b"></attribute>
<attribute name="briefOutline" nodeId="29929a3e">&lt;p&gt;
    Impact assessments can show:
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Description of the current state
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Description of the future state
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Description of the impact(s)
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Severity of impact(s)
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Mitigating actions
    &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;</attribute>
